From 384eca19b59f47d546cfca4445786e0b3e03fc95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shyalya <shyalya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:07:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Replace the premade talent specs and tie them to the
 assigned role

Turtle reworked every talent tree, so all 94 stock links are rejected at startup and bots run around with no talents at all. Replaced with 22 hand-built level 60 specs - one per role for every class, three for druid, paladin, mage and warlock - each with a levelling path every five levels. Without those intermediate entries a level 20 bot gets handed the level 60 link and, since talents are applied in tree order, spends its first points in the secondary tree.

ChangeTalentsAction passed BOT_ROLE_NONE and picked at random among the class builds, so a bot sent to tank could end up with a caster build. It now reads the role the dungeon finder assigned; LFT_ROLE_* and BotRoles share their bit values, so no conversion is needed.

Druid feral now counts as tank rather than dps in GetPlayerRoles. The dungeon finder does put druids on the tank slot, and this mapping is what decides which build they are given.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../PlayerBots/playerbot/AiFactory.cpp        |   8 +-
 .../playerbot/aiplayerbot.conf.dist.in        | 551 ++++++++++--------
 .../strategy/actions/ChangeTalentsAction.cpp  |   4 +-
 3 files changed, 329 insertions(+), 234 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/AiFactory.cpp b/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/AiFactory.cpp
index 82b1e9c..b393fd6 100644
--- a/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/AiFactory.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/AiFactory.cpp
@@ -235,7 +235,11 @@ BotRoles AiFactory::GetPlayerRoles(uint8 cls, uint8 tab)
             }
             else if (tab == 1)
             {
-                role = BOT_ROLE_DPS;
+                // Feral counts as tank here. The dungeon finder can put a druid
+                // on the tank slot, and this mapping decides which premade
+                // talent build it gets - with DPS it would be handed a balance
+                // build and try to tank in caster form.
+                role = BOT_ROLE_TANK;
             }
             else if (tab == 2)
             {
@@ -724,6 +728,7 @@ void AiFactory::AddDefaultCombatStrategies(Player* player, PlayerbotAI* const fa
             combatEngine->addStrategies("behind", "stealth", "poisons", "buff", NULL);
         }
     }
+
 }
 
 Engine* AiFactory::createCombatEngine(Player* player, PlayerbotAI* const facade, AiObjectContext* AiObjectContext)
@@ -1159,6 +1164,7 @@ void AiFactory::AddDefaultNonCombatStrategies(Player* player, PlayerbotAI* const
 #endif
         }
     }
+
 }
 
 Engine* AiFactory::createNonCombatEngine(Player* player, PlayerbotAI* const facade, AiObjectContext* AiObjectContext) 
